# A day between a client and a venue, both directions
#
# PRODCLI -> PRODVENUE: orders (D), a replace (G), cancels (F) and a DK (Q).
# PRODVENUE -> PRODCLI: ExecutionReports (8) -- acks, fills, a replace, a cancel,
# a reject, a re-notified fill after the DK, an end-of-day expiry -- and
# one OrderCancelReject (9).
#
# Play the client's side into an initiator, or the venue's into an acceptor:
# Start asks which. Logons, heartbeats, the test request and the logouts
# are in the file and never sent. PRD-3 carries routing tags (50, 57, 115)
# and a Parties group, which go out as logged; the lunch gap before PRD-9
# is where `max gap` applies.
